message:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - Build complete software stack for ExCELLsis, a portable edge-AI cellular bioanalysis device for TSA Biotechnology nationals running on Raspberry Pi 5 + Hailo-10H NPU
   - Create full repo scaffold (Python backend modules with correct signatures)
   - Build/run a UI preview on Windows (localhost) — discovered existing React web app in GitHub repo, cloned and ran that instead of building OpenCV UI
   - Tune the React UI's mock cell simulation (size, count, movement, overlap)
   - Implement GPIO 27 button → WebSocket → React mode cycling system so judges can switch display modes without a touchscreen
   - Achieve real-time cell visualization: judges swab their cheek, insert slide, watch AI detect their own cells live
   - No liquids allowed (TSA competition rule) — this is an UNRESOLVED constraint discovered at the end of the conversation

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Raspberry Pi 5 + Hailo-10H NPU (PCIe, AI HAT+ 2, 40 TOPS INT4)
   - YOLOv5n compiled to INT4 HEF format for Hailo-10H (NOT compatible with Hailo-8)
   - React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS frontend (existing repo: CellSight UI)
   - MockAIService simulating ~30 drifting cells at ~12fps with spring physics
   - WebSocket server (Python `websockets` library, asyncio, daemon thread, port 8765)
   - GPIO 17 = chamber light toggle, GPIO 27 = display mode cycle (new button needed)
   - Mode cycling: DETECTION → HEATMAP → DENSITY MAP → RAW FEED (press 'M' on dev)
   - Chromium kiosk mode for Pi deployment (planned)
   - IMX477 HQ Camera has C-mount thread → compatible with microscope objectives
   - Cheek cells (~50-100μm) require staining + trans-illumination + objective for visibility
   - No liquids allowed per TSA competition rules (CRITICAL unresolved constraint)
   - CSI = (abnormal/total) × mean_confidence × 100; Health Score = max(0, min(100, round(100 - CSI×3)))

3. Files and Code Sections:

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\src\gpio_control.py** — Completely rewritten to add GPIO 27:
   ```python
   class GPIOController:
       def __init__(self, chamber_pin=17, mode_pin=27, on_mode_press=None):
           # Both pins with pull-up, debounce 50ms
           GPIO.add_event_detect(mode_pin, GPIO.FALLING,
               callback=self._on_mode_btn_press, bouncetime=50)
       def _on_mode_btn_press(self, channel):
           if self._on_mode_press:
               self._on_mode_press()
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\src\websocket_server.py** — New file, WebSocket bridge:
   ```python
   def broadcast_sync(msg: dict) -> None:
       """Thread-safe: call from any thread to push msg to all UI clients."""
       if _loop and _loop.is_running():
           asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe(_broadcast(msg), _loop)

   def start() -> None:
       t = threading.Thread(target=_run, daemon=True, name="ws-server")
       t.start()
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\src\main.py** — Updated to start WebSocket + wire GPIO 27:
   ```python
   websocket_server.start()
   def on_mode_press():
       websocket_server.broadcast_sync({"event": "mode_cycle"})
   gpio = GPIOController(on_mode_press=on_mode_press)
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\ui\src\services\wsClient.ts** — New WebSocket client:
   ```typescript
   export class WSClient {
     constructor() { this.connect(); }
     private connect() {
       this.ws = new WebSocket("ws://localhost:8765");
       this.ws.onclose = () => setTimeout(() => this.connect(), 2000);
       this.ws.onerror = () => {}; // silent fail during dev
     }
     subscribe(handler: Handler): () => void { ... }
   }
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\ui\src\App.tsx** — Added mode cycling + WSClient:
   ```typescript
   const ws = useMemo(() => new WSClient(), []);
   const MODES = [
     { boxes: true,  heatmap: false, label: "DETECTION"   },
     { boxes: true,  heatmap: true,  label: "HEATMAP"     },
     { boxes: false, heatmap: true,  label: "DENSITY MAP" },
     { boxes: false, heatmap: false, label: "RAW FEED"    },
   ] as const;
   const [modeIdx, setModeIdx] = useState(0);
   const cycleMode = () => setModeIdx((i) => (i + 1) % MODES.length);
   // WebSocket + 'M' key listener
   useEffect(() => {
     const offWs = ws.subscribe((msg) => {
       if (msg.event === "mode_cycle") cycleMode();
     });
     const onKey = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
       if (e.key === "m" || e.key === "M") cycleMode();
     };
     window.addEventListener("keydown", onKey);
     return () => { offWs(); window.removeEventListener("keydown", onKey); };
   }, [ws]);
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\ui\src\components\LiveFeed.tsx** — Updated props, single cycle button:
   ```typescript
   interface Props {
     frame: InferenceFrame | null;
     showBoxes: boolean;
     showHeatmap: boolean;
     modeLabel: string;      // new
     onCycleMode: () => void; // replaces onToggleBoxes + onToggleHeatmap
   }
   // Header button now shows current mode name and cycles on click
   ```

   **C:\Users\busyp\excellsis\ui\src\services\mockAI.ts** — Cell simulation tuned:
   ```typescript
   function spawnPopulation(n: number, existing: Cell[] = []): Cell[] {
     // retry loop — places cells without overlap
     const w = rand(0.055, 0.09); // bigger cells
     // overlap check using circle distance
     const overlaps = [...existing, ...cells].some(c => {
       const dx = cx - ocx, dy = cy - ocy;
       return Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy) < r + or2 + 0.005;
     });
   }
   // tick() adds separation physics:
   if (dist < minDist) {
     const push = (minDist - dist) / 2;
     a.x -= nx * push; b.x += nx * push; // etc.
   }
   // velocity: rand(-0.00008, 0.00008) — 10x slower
   // default cell count: 30
   ```

